WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:00.922
- When cooking
(fun jazzy music)

00:00:00.922 --> 00:00:02.221
in the kitchen, it's very important

00:00:02.221 --> 00:00:03.788
to use the best tools for the job.

00:00:03.788 --> 00:00:07.181
This will ensure maximum flavor
as well as optimal textures.

00:00:07.181 --> 00:00:08.826
Hi, my name's Alexis, and today

00:00:08.826 --> 00:00:10.044
we're going to talk about the difference

00:00:10.044 --> 00:00:11.852
between three common household pans.

00:00:11.852 --> 00:00:13.626
Let's start with the nonstick pan.

00:00:13.626 --> 00:00:16.273
This is probably the most
common pan for beginner cooks.

00:00:16.273 --> 00:00:17.841
These are fairly inexpensive, and due

00:00:17.841 --> 00:00:20.227
to their nonstick surface,
they're super easy to clean.

00:00:20.227 --> 00:00:22.700
To increase the longevity of
your pan, you need to ensure

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:25.016
that you're taking proper
care of the nonstick surface.

00:00:25.016 --> 00:00:27.036
For example, when you're
making scrambled eggs,

00:00:27.036 --> 00:00:29.718
you should always be using
silicone or wooden tools.

00:00:29.718 --> 00:00:31.825
And that goes for all
other dishes as well.

00:00:31.825 --> 00:00:34.141
To get the best results
from your nonstick pan,

00:00:34.141 --> 00:00:35.918
we recommend you cook delicate dishes

00:00:35.918 --> 00:00:38.162
like eggs, pancakes, grilled cheese,

00:00:38.162 --> 00:00:40.635
and lighter fish such as tilapia.

00:00:40.635 --> 00:00:42.324
Proteins like steak, chicken thighs,

00:00:42.324 --> 00:00:45.372
burgers, or salmon aren't
ideal for a nonstick pan,

00:00:45.372 --> 00:00:47.235
as those require high heat.

00:00:47.235 --> 00:00:48.924
If you're looking for easy cleanup

00:00:48.924 --> 00:00:50.141
and don't wanna make dishes that require

00:00:50.141 --> 00:00:52.074
high heat, this is the pan for you.

00:00:52.074 --> 00:00:53.920
So now let's talk about cast-irons.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.992
I think everybody should
own one of these pans.

00:00:55.992 --> 00:00:58.343
Cast-iron pans are
exceptionally versatile.

00:00:58.343 --> 00:00:59.980
These sturdy pans can be used

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:02.384
on the stovetop as well as in the oven.

00:01:02.384 --> 00:01:04.247
Cast-iron pans are not only affordable,

00:01:04.247 --> 00:01:05.762
but if you take proper care of them,

00:01:05.762 --> 00:01:07.016
they can last for decades.

00:01:07.016 --> 00:01:08.740
These long-lasting pans can be used

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:10.847
to cook an array of dishes, from steak,

00:01:10.847 --> 00:01:13.146
fruit cobbler, and even frittata.

00:01:13.146 --> 00:01:15.706
You can cook nearly everything
with a cast-iron pan,

00:01:15.706 --> 00:01:18.876
but for beginner cooks,
they may seem intimidating.

00:01:18.876 --> 00:01:21.314
Pans need to be treated
before their first use,

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:26.169
and the cleanup is more involved
than with a nonstick pan.

00:01:26.169 --> 00:01:27.653
If you're willing to do the cleanup,

00:01:27.653 --> 00:01:30.840
cast-iron pans are a worthwhile
addition to any kitchen.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:33.226
Now let's talk about
our third and final pan.

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:34.671
Stainless steel is without a doubt

00:01:34.671 --> 00:01:36.413
my favorite pan to use in the kitchen.

00:01:36.413 --> 00:01:38.746
These pans are built
tough, and like cast-iron,

00:01:38.746 --> 00:01:41.184
can be used on the
stovetop or in the oven.

00:01:41.184 --> 00:01:42.386
They're particularly good

00:01:42.386 --> 00:01:44.232
when you want a nice sear on a protein.

00:01:44.232 --> 00:01:47.210
You can truly cook everything
with a stainless steel pan:

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:51.215
salmon, sauteed vegetables,
risotto, and even eggs.

00:01:51.215 --> 00:01:53.758
The fear around using
the stainless steel pan

00:01:53.758 --> 00:01:55.464
is the idea that food will stick.

00:01:55.464 --> 00:01:57.720
To prevent this, you need
to make sure you're using

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:00.545
a pre-heated pan and the
appropriate amount of oil.

00:02:00.545 --> 00:02:02.809
So, here I have two chicken
thighs, and I'm gonna show you

00:02:02.809 --> 00:02:04.043
just how easy it is
(clattering)

00:02:04.043 --> 00:02:05.750
to make sure your food doesn't stick.

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:08.223
First things first,
let's pre-heat the pan.

00:02:08.223 --> 00:02:10.243
I'm going to add about
two teaspoons of oil,

00:02:10.243 --> 00:02:12.385
just enough to coat the bottom of the pan.

00:02:12.385 --> 00:02:13.830
Once the oil begins to shimmer,

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:16.759
I'm going to add the seasoned
chicken, skin side down.

00:02:16.759 --> 00:02:19.009
(sizzling)

00:02:20.436 --> 00:02:21.760
I'm going to let the chicken rest

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:23.493
in the pan for a few minutes.

00:02:23.493 --> 00:02:25.191
Once the chicken begins to pull away

00:02:25.191 --> 00:02:28.936
from the pan, it should be ready to flip.

00:02:28.936 --> 00:02:29.769
See?!

00:02:29.769 --> 00:02:30.839
It's so easy.

00:02:30.839 --> 00:02:33.466
Check out that beautiful golden skin.

00:02:33.466 --> 00:02:35.208
I'm going to let them brown
for a few more minutes

00:02:35.208 --> 00:02:36.688
on the other side, and then I'm going

00:02:36.688 --> 00:02:39.271
to finish them off in the oven.

00:02:40.638 --> 00:02:42.536
After you remove the
chicken from the oven,

00:02:42.536 --> 00:02:43.911
there's going to be some brown bits

00:02:43.911 --> 00:02:45.217
at the bottom of the pan.

00:02:45.217 --> 00:02:46.711
This is called the foundation.

00:02:46.711 --> 00:02:48.835
At this point, you can go
ahead and scrub the pan,

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:50.820
or what I prefer to do is take advantage

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:53.049
of the amazing flavor from the chicken fat

00:02:53.049 --> 00:02:55.278
and make a really simple pan sauce.

00:02:55.278 --> 00:02:56.584
Reduce the stock for a few minutes,

00:02:56.584 --> 00:03:00.751
then add garlic, thyme, and
a bit of butter, and stir.

00:03:01.791 --> 00:03:03.443
Pour the sauce over the
chicken and you've got

00:03:03.443 --> 00:03:06.526
a great, easy dinner and a clean pan.

00:03:08.093 --> 00:03:09.957
So, as you can see, stainless steel

00:03:09.957 --> 00:03:13.015
can do everything that a
nonstick and a cast-iron can do.

00:03:13.015 --> 00:03:17.182
In my opinion, it's the most
versatile pan out there.

